8:3: forma-kind: `icon.theme`: an icon token is declared under `icons`
9:20: forma-kind: `icon.dup` is an icon: a `symbol:` source names it, not a value
13:3: forma-duplicate: `ink` is declared twice
15:3: forma-duplicate: `icon.dup` is declared twice
16:3: forma-kind: `icon.kind`: an `icons` block holds icon tokens
17:3: forma-icon-axis: `icon.varies`: an icon has one source per platform, so no `when` (vary the row's symbol instead)
19:19: forma-kind: an icon has an `sf` or an `svg` source: a `material` name is an annotation, which no host draws
20:17: forma-kind: `../star.svg`: an SVG is a `.svg` file under the app's `assets/`, by its path there (`icons/reply.svg`)
21:14: forma-kind: `png`: an icon's sources are `sf`, `material` and `svg`
22:15: forma-kind: an icon is `icon(sf "…", material "…", svg "…")`
23:3: forma-icon-name: `star`: an icon's name is dotted (`icon.star`), so no dial, role or CSS word is spelled as one
24:16: forma-kind: an icon has an `sf` or an `svg` source: `icon(sf "bubble.left")`
25:18: forma-kind: `..\outside.svg`: an SVG is a `.svg` file under the app's `assets/`, by its path there (`icons/reply.svg`)
26:16: forma-kind: `C:/outside.svg`: an SVG is a `.svg` file under the app's `assets/`, by its path there (`icons/reply.svg`)
